.TH SOUND 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
Sound \- A decoded .wav held in memory, ready to play any number of times
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqaudio.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct Sound { Uint8 *data; Uint32 len; SDL_AudioSpec spec; } Sound;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A decoded .wav held in memory, ready to play any number of times. Returned by audio_load(); freed by audio_free(). Holds a pointer, so it belongs in a scene static (load in on_enter, free in on_exit), never in GameState. A zero Sound (failed load) is safe to pass everywhere and plays silence.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B data
the samples
.TP
.B len
size of data in bytes
.TP
.B spec
sample format, channels and rate, as stored in the file
.SH MODULE
audio (src/engine/audio/audio.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR audio_load (3),
.BR audio_play (3),
.BR audio_music (3),
.BR audio_free (3),
.BR gge\-audio (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
